    "text": "Modern large language model (LLM) agents interacting with each other often exhibit myopic and polarized interaction patterns, leading to suboptimal coordination and increased regret.",
    "topic": "Multi-Agent Exploration"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Multi-Agent Exploration problem is formalized as a partially observable stochastic game (POSG) where agents must probe peers to infer capabilities and identify effective interaction strategies.",
    "topic": "Multi-Agent Exploration"
  },
  {
    "text": "Multi-Agent Contextual Exploration (MACE) is a lightweight framework that explicitly promotes exploration through structured peer selection, improving exploration behavior and downstream task performance across diverse settings.",
    "topic": "MACE Framework"
  },
  {
    "text": "Theoretical analysis shows that the value of exploration increases with agent diversity in multi-agent systems.",
    "topic": "Agent Diversity and Exploration"
  },
  {
    "text": "Current LLM agents have a fundamental limitation in their ability to explore each other effectively, highlighting the importance of explicitly guided exploration for reliable multi-agent autonomy.",
    "topic": "Limitations of LLM Agents"
  }
]
